Assuming you are running the 3.4.3 game version, you and I are playing
the same game (Mac Qt) on the same OS version (10.4.6). The only time
I've seen anything like the symptom you describe is when I've renamed
or moved the tiles file, or specified the wrong tile height/width. But
I've not seen any change in behavior obviously related to running on
Mac OS 10.4.x, sorry.

Are you getting any display -- a window caption, status information,
the message scroll, anything? Is it possible the window is displaying
beyond your display boundary? If so, Expose should reveal it.

Oh, one more thing: The Mac OS X Qt game does not use ".nethackrc" as
the preferences file, probably because "." files are not Finder
friendly. It instead uses one these files:

    ~/Library/Preferences/NetHack Defaults
    ~/Library/Preferences/NetHack Defaults.txt

